/* =============================================================================
 * syz_tok_tables.h — SYZT v0 learned tone codebooks (GENERATED, do not edit)
 * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Generated by syzygy-forge from tables/table_micro.json / table_full.json.
 * Trained by integer k-means (T1) on the docks corpus — see the forge README.
 *
 * Selection (the inference form frozen here):
 *     sel = argmax_j ( <inference_rows_j, feat> + inference_bias_j )
 * which is exactly nearest-centroid over `rows`, since
 * inference_rows_j = 2*rows_j and inference_bias_j = -||rows_j||^2.
 * First maximum wins, mirroring syz_ste_select's tie rule.
 *
 * Table id = FNV-1a/32 over the centroid rows serialised as little-endian
 * int32, row-major. A (kernel, table, frame) triple names a result.
 * With no table selected, the kernel's existing outputs are unchanged.
 * ========================================================================== */
